## Canonical sources of truth

- **Bland.ai IDs** (pathways, KB, voice, tools, webhooks, Cal.com): `b2b_sales_enablement/bland_ai_pathways/canonical_ids.json`
- **Frontend ID mirror**: `superpatch-frontend/src/lib/config/pathways.ts`
- **Edge Function ID mirror**: `superpatch-frontend/supabase/functions/_shared/pathways.ts`
- **Supabase schema snapshot**: `superpatch-frontend/supabase/schema.sql`
- **DB types mirror**: `superpatch-frontend/src/lib/db/types.ts`

A Vitest test (`canonical-ids-sync.test.ts`) enforces that the three ID mirrors stay aligned.

## Primary data flow (E2E)

```
Places/Firecrawl/LinkedIn
       |
       v
Supabase practitioners (+ enrichment JSONB)
       |
       v
batch-caller / process-retry-queue (Edge Functions)
       |
       v   [Bland.ai call with pathway_id + KB + request_data]
Bland pathway (per practitioner type)
       |
       v   [extractVars + tool invocations]
webhook-processor (Edge Function)
       |
       +--> sample_requests (Resend email)
       |
       +--> book-appointment Edge Function (Cal.com)
       |
       +--> call_records (transcript, outcomes)
       |
       v
Next.js UI (/campaign, analytics, follow-up queue)
```

See `ARCHITECTURE.md` for the full diagram and `LEAD_PIPELINE.md` for the ingestion side.

## Stack (as of 2026-04)

- **Frontend**: Next.js 16.1.1 (App Router), React 19.2.3, shadcn/ui, Tailwind v4, Supabase SSR, Vercel
- **Backend**: Supabase Edge Functions (Deno), Supabase Postgres, pg_net, pg_cron
- **Voice AI**: Bland.ai pathways (v1 API) with Cal.com custom tools
- **Scheduling**: Cal.com v1/v2
- **Email**: Resend
- **AI analysis**: Google Gemini (transcript analysis)
- **Python tooling**: 3.12+ (scraping, pathway authoring, Flask appointment webhook)

## Scope guidance

- Never create files in the repo root for application code. Frontend code belongs in `superpatch-frontend/`. Backend / Edge Function / Python work belongs under `superpatch-frontend/supabase/`, `b2b_sales_enablement/`, or `scripts/`.
- Check `canonical_ids.json` before hardcoding any Bland / Cal.com / KB / voice / tool ID.
- Check existing Edge Functions (`superpatch-frontend/supabase/functions/`) before writing new ones — many utilities already exist (`webhook-processor`, `process-retry-queue`, `enrich-practitioners-v2`, `book-appointment`, `send-sample-confirmation`, `sync-cal-bookings`).
